# Project Rules for Cursor

Canonical specs (read first on each edit):
- /docs/agent-prd.md
- /docs/architecture.md

Contracts
- Honor the JSON contract in /lib/schemas/workout.ts (use validateWorkoutPlan before persisting).
- Keep business rules in /lib/workout.ts (main-lift selection, cooldown matching, time trimming).

Engineering constraints
- TypeScript strict; no unused imports/vars; build must pass.
- Enforce strict JSON from LLM; invalid → HTTP 400 (do not persist).
- UI renders JSON; no free-text parsing for plans.
- Read profile & equipment via profiles → user_equipment → equipment join.
- strength starts with main/core lift (except HIIT). Accessories explicitly flagged.
- Cooldowns must match focus muscles; never generic/mismatched.
- Time-boxing: cut accessories first, then trim main-lift volume.
- No equipment → bodyweight plan.
- Save to workout_sessions & workout_sets only on Finish with workout_source tag when available.
- Maintain one active chat_sessions row; archive overflow to workout_chat_log; rebuild request context from DB.
- Coach message: motivational, max 2 sentences.

When modifying code
- Reference /docs/agent-prd.md + /docs/architecture.md in PRs/commits.
- Prefer mini spec + unified patch; keep diffs surgical and self-contained.
